# rsync protections for deploy/analytics -> /opt/analytics.
#
# Read by deploy/tofu/scripts/analytics-rsync.sh through rsync --exclude-from.
# Blank lines and whole-line `#` comments are ignored (GNU rsync man page for
# --exclude-from; verified against macOS openrsync too). Patterns have no rule
# prefix, so every rule here is an exclude - which means each protected path is
# exempt from --delete as well as from being overwritten.
#
# Keep the final newline. A last pattern on an unterminated final line is dropped
# by openrsync (macOS), which silently un-protects the path.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE COMPLETE PROTECTED SET. Add a pattern here when a path in
# /opt/analytics must survive a sync, with a reason. Deletions the sync is
# expected to make belong in analytics-delete-allowlist.txt instead; the script
# prints and checks that list before it deletes anything.
#
# .env           installed 0600 by null_resource.install_envs (stacks.tf also
#                reinstalls it right after the sync) and holds the analytics
#                secrets. Syncing the repo's .env over it would be a leak.
# *.before-*     hand-made "what was here before this change" copies. The
#                pattern is `.before-`, not `*bak-*`: a filter pattern with no
#                `/` in it matches trailing path components only and `*` does
#                not cross `/`, so `*.before-*` cannot match `compose.yaml.bak-`.
# *.bak-*        those same copies under the other name used on the host.
#                Verified locally: with only `*.before-*` present, rsync lists
#                every compose.yaml.bak-* in the destination as `*deleting`.
# dags-disabled  Airflow DAGs the operator disabled by moving them aside. The
#                `dags` directory itself IS synced, so only the moved subtree
#                must be hidden.
.env
*.before-*
*.bak-*
dags-disabled
